prompt_template:
Create a {ASPECT_RATIO} image in the "urban-photo-ink-beast-collage-style" visual style.

Subject: {SUBJECT}
Action: {SUBJECT_ACTION}
Prop/Product: {PRODUCT_OR_PROP}
Location: {LOCATION}
Background: {BACKGROUND_ELEMENTS}
Main text: {MAIN_TEXT}
Secondary text: {SECONDARY_TEXT}
Accent symbol: {ACCENT_SYMBOL}
Wardrobe/styling: {WARDROBE_STYLE}
Style fidelity anchors: {STYLE_FIDELITY_ANCHORS}
Source content to avoid: {SOURCE_CONTENT_TO_AVOID}

Apply these style rules:
- Composition: place a softly faded full-bleed architectural photograph behind one monumental black-dominant illustrated beast occupying roughly half the frame. Pair it asymmetrically with one much smaller theatrical figure. Use a low street-level or upward-looking photographic perspective, keep 15 to 25 percent open sky or pale architecture, boldly crop the giant form, and place no more than three tiny abstract glyphs in the open area.
- Material split: the city must look genuinely photographed with analog grain and natural daylight, while every narrative subject, costume, prop, and symbol must look like opaque flat paper and hand ink pasted on top. Preserve the deliberate mismatch; do not blend the illustration into the photo.
- Drawing: use broad near-solid black and paper-white masses, thick uneven wobbling contours, abrupt cut-paper silhouettes, mask-like eyes and mouths, and wiry loops, hairs, curls, ticks, and short dash textures. Keep volume flat with almost no cast shadows.
- Typography: use no main headline and no secondary copy unless the case explicitly requests it. Never create a headline band, speech bubble, or editorial text grid.
- Color: keep the photograph faded blue-gray, tan, and brick. Let black and white dominate the illustrated area; use cobalt blue and vermilion red sparingly, plus one sweeping lemon-yellow accent and only a trace of blush pink.
- Graphic elements: add up to three small hand-drawn rod-and-loop glyphs, circular targets, motion curls, or wing-like strokes in the sky. These marks must remain abstract and must not resemble aircraft.
- Mood: experimental editorial photomontage, absurd theatrical humor, playful menace, and late-20th-century underground magazine energy.

Avoid: giant apes or gorillas, captive or screaming women, aircraft, New York landmarks, the source pose or story, photoreal monsters, cinematic integration, 3D rendering, clean vector art, manga, comic panels, children's-book softness, large typography, logos, QR codes, watermarks, usernames, platform marks, app UI, famous characters, and copied identity marks.

Important content rule: match the photo-versus-flat-ink style, scale hierarchy, palette behavior, scribbled line treatment, and sparse glyph grammar first; then change every literal subject, action, prop, location, costume, and story detail from the source.
